{"strongs": "H3245", "word": "יָסַד", "translit": "ya.sad", "root": "יסד", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "establish, found, fix", "definition": "יָסַד verb establish, found, fix (Late Hebrew id. , especially Pi`el; Aramaic יְסַד ; perhaps originally fix firm or close ; Arabic pillow ; verb denominative II. fix as a pillow against one ; see lean against, recline , Lane 2940 Saad Gen 28:11 in Hebrew usually fix firm so as to found ) — Qal Perfect יָסַד Ps 104:5 ; Prov 3:19 suffix יְסָדָהּ Ps 24:2 + 3 t.; 3 feminine singular יָסְדָה Isa 48:13 יָסַדְתָּ Ps 104:8 יָסַ֑֫דְתָּ Ps 102:26 suffix יְסַדְתּוֺ Hab 1:12 יְסַדְתָּם Ps 89:12 ; Ps 119:152 וִיסַדְתִּיךְ consecutive Isa 54:11 Infinitive וִיסוֺד 2Chr 24:27 לִיסּוֺד 2Chr 31:7 (see Ges «GKC:69»§ 69 , 2, R. 1; Baer לְיִסּוֺד ); לִיסֹד Isa 51:16 יָסְדִי Job 38:4 יָסְדוֺ Ezra 3:12 Participle יִסֵד Isa 51:13 ; Zech 12:1 + Isa 28:16 ( Che critical note , ᵑ0 יִסַּד ); — found, establish , with accusative, the earth Ps 24:2 (|| כונן ), compare Ps 78:69 (object omitted), Ps 89:12 ; Ps 102:26 ; Ps 104:5 compare v Ps 89:8 (followed by לְ ), Prov 3:19 ; Isa 48:13 ; Job 38:4 ; Isa 51:13 ; Isa 51:16 ; Zech 12:1 , vault of heaven Amos 9:6 of founding the second temple Ezra 3:12 , of restoration under Joash, Infinitive יְסוֺד 2Chr 24:27 metaphor of future Israel Isa 54:11 of ׳ י , establish the Chaldaean (as his instrument) להוכיח for correction Hab 1:12 (|| שִׁים ), his commandments Ps 119:152 in weakened sense (si vera lectio) יָסַד לְצִיִּים Isa 23:13 appoint a city for desert-creatures (on meaning in context, see Di ); appoint, fix Ezra 7:9 emended (see יְסֻד ); found, begin , heaps of offerings in ׳ י 's house 2Chr 31:7 . Niph`al Perfect 3 plural נוֺסְְדוּ Ps 2:2 Imperfect 2 masculine singular תִּוָּסֵד Isa 44:28 Infinitive הִוָּסְדָהּ Exod 9:18 הִיָּסְדָם Ps 31:14 — 1. fix or seat themselves close together sit in conclave Ps 2:2 ; Ps 31:14 ( > Bae from , δμιλιἀ ), but Lag's emendation נוֺעֲדוּ is probably (compare Neh 6:2 ). 2. be founded , Isa 44:28 (temple), Exod 9:18 (Egypt). Pi`el Perfect יִסַּד Isa 14:32 + 3 t.; יִסְּדָהּ 1Kgs 16:34 יִסַּ֫דְתָּ Ps 8:3 יִסְּדוּ Zech 4:9 ; Ezra 3:10 Imperfect יְיַסְּדֶנָּה Josh 6:26 Infinitive לְיַסֵּד 1Kgs 5:31 — 1. found (= Qal ), followed by active, city Josh 6:26 ( J E ), 1Kgs 16:34 , temple 1Kgs 5:31 ; Zech 4:9 ; Ezra 3:10 Zion Isa 14:32 ; Isa 28:16 הִנְנִי יִסַּד (read יֹסֵד ; see above) 2. establish Ps 8:3 followed by עֹז ; appoint, ordain (late) 1Chr 9:22 (followed by accusative), Esth 1:8 (absolute) Pu`al Perfect , יֻסַּד 1Kgs 6:37 + 2 t.; יֻסָּ֑ד Ezra 3:6 Participle מְיסָֻּ֑ד 1Kgs 7:10 מְיסָֻּדִים Song 5:15 be founded, be laid, of a foundation 1Kgs 6:37 ; Ezra 3:6 ; Hag 2:18 ; Zech 8:9 Participle = substantive foundation 1Kgs 7:10 , compare מוסד below; pillars set on bases, simile of legs Song 5:15 . Hoph`al be founded: Infinitive הוּסַד 2Chr 3:3 ; Ezra 3:11 Participle מוּסָּד Isa 28:16 — the being founded, founding , ׳ עַל הוּסַד בֵּית י Ezra 3:11 because of the founding (laying the foundation) of the house of ׳ י ; וְאֵלֶּה ׳ הוּסַד שְׁלֹמֹה לִבְנוֺת וגו 2Chr 3:3 and this is (literally these are) the founding of Solomon to build the house of God, i.e. this is the foundation which Solomon laid for building , etc.; Participle מוּסָד מוּסָּד Isa 28:16 a foundation founded , i.e. well laid (compare חֵפֶשׂ מְחֻפָּשׂ , חָכָם מְחֻכָּם ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3589')\">BDB3589</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3245')\">H3245</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3588')\">BDB3588</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3590')\">BDB3590</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יָסַד</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>establish, found, fix</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>, especially Pi`el; Aramaic <bdbarc>יְסַד</bdbarc>; perhaps originally <highlight>fix firm</highlight> or <highlight>close</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder2238/> <highlight>pillow</highlight>; ve